            "title": "Relative changes in oxyhemoglobin, deoxyhemoglobin and intracranial blood volume during surfactant replacement therapy in infants with respiratory distress syndrome.",
            "abstract": "Oxy-, deoxyhemoglobin and total blood volume were studied by near-infrared spectroscopy (NIRS) during surfactant replacement therapy. These parameters were compared with parameters watched during conventional noninvasive monitoring (pulseoximetry, transcutaneous pO2 and pCO2, heart rate). Seven premature infants (28 +/- 3 weeks of gestation, 940 g birth weight) were given surfactant intratracheally. Immediately after surfactant administration, oxyhemoglobin decreased, deoxyhemoglobin and total blood volume increased. The prior status was re-established after 60-220 s and then oxyhemoglobin increased to a very stable maximum. NIRS allows continuous bedside noninvasive monitoring of all parameters.",
