            "field_name": "gestational_age_severity",
            "label": "Gestational age severity of enrolled infants",
            "description": "Study-level prematurity severity based on the gestational age eligibility criteria or dominant enrolled population.",
            "reason": "Gestational age thresholds and strata were repeatedly reported across trials and follow-up studies, commonly distinguishing extremely preterm infants below 26, 28, or 29 weeks from broader very preterm or preterm populations. This field is likely extractable and may affect baseline risk and applicability of mortality, brain injury, oxygenation, and neurodevelopmental outcomes.",
