            "nct_text": "ClinicalTrials.gov record: NCT03770741\nURL: https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT03770741\nAcronym: SafeBoosC\nBrief title: Safeguarding the Brain of Our Smallest Infants Phase III\nOfficial title: Safeguarding the Brain of Our Smallest Children - an Investigator-initiated, Pragmatic, Open Label, Multinational Randomized Phase IIIclinical Trial Evaluating Treatment Based on Near-infrared Spectroscopy Monitoring Versus Treatment as Usual in Premature Infants\nOverall status: COMPLETED\nStudy type: INTERVENTIONAL\nPhases: NA\nConditions: Infant, Extremely Premature, Brain Injuries, Death, Brain, Death; Neonatal\nHas posted results: False\n\nBrief summary:\nthe SafeBoosC-III trial investigates the benefit and harms of treatment based on near-infrared spectroscopy monitoring compared with treatment as usual. The hypothesis is that treatment based on near-infrared spectroscopy monitoring for extremely preterm infants during the first 72 hours of life will result in a reduction in severe brain injury or death at 36 weeks postmenstrual age.\n\nArms/groups:\n[\n  {\n    \"label\": \"Monitoring of cerebral oxygenation\",\n    \"type\": \"EXPERIMENTAL\",\n    \"description\": \"Modify cardio-respiratory support to avoid cerebral hypoxia\",\n    \"interventionNames\": [\n      \"Other: Modify cardio-respiratory support to avoid cerebral hypoxia\"\n    ]\n  },\n  {\n    \"label\": \"Treatment as usual\",\n    \"type\": \"OTHER\",\n    \"description\": \"Treatment according local guidelines and practices.\",\n    \"interventionNames\": [\n      \"Other: Treatment as usual\"\n    ]\n  }\n]\n\nInterventions:\n[\n  {\n    \"type\": \"OTHER\",\n    \"name\": \"Modify cardio-respiratory support to avoid cerebral hypoxia\",\n    \"description\": \"modification of cardio-respiratory support based on an evidence-based treatment guideline\",\n    \"armGroupLabels\": [\n      \"Monitoring of cerebral oxygenation\"\n    ]\n  },\n  {\n    \"type\": \"OTHER\",\n    \"name\": \"Treatment as usual\",\n    \"description\": \"Monitoring and treatment according to local guidelines and practice\",\n    \"armGroupLabels\": [\n      \"Treatment as usual\"\n    ]\n  }\n]\n\nProtocol primary outcomes:\n[\n  {\n    \"measure\": \"Severe brain injury or death\",\n    \"time_frame\": \"From birth to 36 weeks postmenstrual age\",\n    \"description\": \"A composite of severe brain injury detected on any one of a series of cranial ultrasound scans that are routinely performed in these infants up to 36 weeks postmenstrual age or death at 36 weeks postmenstrual age\"\n  }\n]"
